DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Semantic tag</title>

    <style>
        *{
            padding: 0%;
            margin: 0%;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }
        nav{
            background-color: darkgoldenrod;
            color: rgb(18, 19, 19);
            height: 80px;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-around;
            align-items: center;
        }
        ul{
            display: flex;
            gap: 20px;
            list-style: none;

        }
        li{
            font-size: 19px;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            font-weight: bold;
            cursor: pointer;
        }
        header{
            height: 250px;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 20px;
            background-color: lightgreen;
        }
        main{
            height: 200px;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            background-color: blueviolet;
        }
        section{
            height: 250px;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            background-color: rgb(210, 115, 115);
        }
        figure{
            border-radius: 15px;
            box-shadow: 0px 8px 15px rgb(53, 49, 49);
            height: 250px;
            width: 350px;
            padding: 15px;
            background-color: rgb(185, 38, 38);
        }
        img{
            border-radius: 15px;
        }
        figcaption{
            text-align: center;
            font-weight: bold;
        }
        article{
            height: 250PX;
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
        }
        aside{
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
        }
        article aside:nth-child(1){
            background-color: rgb(230, 126, 188);
        }
        article aside:nth-child(2){
            background-color: rgb(85, 104, 225);
        }footer{
            height: 100px;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            background-color: chocolate;
        }
        
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <nav>
        <h2>My logo</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>home</li>
            <li>about</li>
            <li>contact</li>
        </ul>
    </nav>
    <header>
        <h1>welcome to semantic tag</h1>
            <p>here we will get to know how to use semantic tag in html and what is the meaning of these tag</p>

       
        <button style="color:red;">Get started</button>
    </header>
    <main>THIS IS MAIN TAG</main>
    <section>
        <figure>
            <img src="https://wordpress.wbur.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/0505_umb-graduation.jpg" alt=""height="180">
        </figure>
            <figcaption> Graduation Day</figcaption>
        </section>
    <article>
        <aside>
            <h2> Collage Event </h2>
        </aside>
        <aside>
            <h2> About Students </h2>
        </aside>
        
    </article>

            <footer>
                <details>
                    <summary>ABOUT OUR COLLEGE</summary>
                    <p> welcome to our collage website. Here you can find information about student events and activities.</p>
                </details>
            </footer>

    
</body>
</html>